{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 280,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do I have to push, sub-basement?\n\u003e\u003eWoman: Sub-basement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3060,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Buzzing safety alarm]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7060,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm at the National Institute of Standards \u0026 Technology\nin Washington D.C."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12220,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I'm going to the sub-basement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14480,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's getting dark down here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're going to find out how they're going to\nredefine a kilogram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21080,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The kilogram is in trouble."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23120,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since 1799, it's been defined as\nthe mass of a metal cylinder,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26620,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a locked vault\nin a basement in Paris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28960,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But over the last century, careful measurements\nof this international prototype kilogram"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33120,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in-theory-identical national standards\nfrom around the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36420,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have shown that their masses are diverging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38980,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The spread has grown to around\n50 micrograms, or 50 parts per billion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43180,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And having a standard of mass that changes\nis unacceptable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47360,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus, the kilogram is the last of the base SI units\nto still be defined by a physical object."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52800,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The metre, for example, used to be defined\nas the length of a platinum bar in Paris,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57040,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but in 1983 it was redefined\nas the distance light travels"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60640,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1/299,792,458 of a second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64980,
    "dDurationMs": 6460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This definition means that the speed of light\nis set to exactly 299,792,458"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71580,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "point 00000..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73540,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "et cetera, metres per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75560,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Note how this works:\nfirst, you take the existing definition,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79220,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say, the length of that metre bar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81180,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you measure as carefully as you can\nhow it relates to a physical constant of the universe:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85780,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87020,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you set the exact value of that constant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90280,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and use *it* to redefine how long a metre is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know this might seem circular,\nbut, importantly, it moves the point of truth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98400,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off of the physical object,\nand onto the unchanging constant of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103660,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, naturally, the thought is\nto do the same thing with the kilogram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But... using which constant, and how?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110060,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Heavy mechanical noises]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115320,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, there are a number of\ndifferent strategies that were attempted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117860,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the two that achieved\nthe greatest success were:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120360,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1) using a silicon sphere to determine and set\nAvogadro's number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124380,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 2) to use a Watt balance\nto determine and set Planck's constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129220,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eDEREK: Hi, how ya' doin'? I'm Derek.\n\u003e\u003eJON: Pretty good.\n\u003e\u003eDEREK: Nice to meet you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131440,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eDEREK: Where is the Watt balance?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132880,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eSTEPHAN: The Watt balance is\nbehind these closed doors, and..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135540,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eDEREK: It's in there?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136460,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eSTEPHAN: It's correct,\nand right now the problem is that..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140060,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are in a crunch to get a number\nby the end of May."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142600,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eDEREK: What's the number?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143740,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eSTEPHAN: The Planck's constant.\nThis is what we measure with the Watt balance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147080,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2011,\nthe General Conference on Weights and Measures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150020,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decided that the kilogram should be redefined\nbased on Planck's constant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153460,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that doesn't mean that\nthe Avogadro approach was futile."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156540,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, you can use Avogadro's number\nto calculate Planck's constant and vice-versa."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160940,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, ultimately, both approaches\nare going to be used to redefine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164100,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Planck's constant and\nAvogadro's number simultaneously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167460,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eSTEPHAN: One good thing about\nhaving silicon spheres,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that you only want to redefine if you have\nagreement between different numbers, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174040,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the silicon sphere method is a method\nin my mind that comes out of chemistry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177680,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You measure Avogadro's constant, which is\na constant that comes out of chemistry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181220,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This method comes out of physics,\nwe measure Planck's constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183680,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if they both agree, it's a pretty strong sign, right?\nBecause you know chemistry and physics agree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187700,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, since I've already discussed the\nAvogadro approach in a previous video,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here I want to focus on the Watt balance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194240,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's actually now called a Kibble balance\nin honor of its inventor, Bryan Kibble,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198860,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who actually passed away in 2016."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, traditional balances work by equating\nthe gravitational forces on objects in two pans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206500,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Kibble balance looks kind of similar,\nbut all of the balancing happens on the left-hand side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211620,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where a mass pan is attached\nto a coil of wire in a magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215260,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the right-hand side is a motor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217580,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole apparatus is sealed\nand operated in vacuum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221040,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The balance operates in two modes:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223200,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Weighing mode and velocity mode,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225640,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and both are required\nto determine Planck's constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228340,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In weighing mode, a kilogram mass standard\nis placed on the mass pan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232380,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then current is passed\nthrough the coil in the magnetic field"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235140,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and adjusted until the weight of\nthe kilogram is equal and opposite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238360,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the electromagnetic\nforce on the coil."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240800,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The equation for this is\nMass times the local gravitational acceleration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244560,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to the Magnetic field, times the length of wire in the coil, times the current flowing through it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250160,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this equation the variables that are difficult to measure exactly are the magnetic field strength, and the length of wire in the coil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257200,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But luckily the Kibble balance allows us to get around this problem using velocity mode"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261900,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In velocity mode the kilogram mass is lifted off the mass pan and now the motor on the other side of the balance is used to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268500,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Move the coil back and forth at constant velocity through the magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272660,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This motion induces a voltage in the coil which is equal to the magnetic field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277100,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times the length of wire in the coil, times its velocity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280280,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we have two equations which we can solve for B times L and so we can set them equal to each other and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286040,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eliminate these variables without having to know precisely what their values are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290120,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if we rearrange a little bit you get voltage times current equals mass times gravity times velocity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296180,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the left hand side, there is electrical power and on the right hand side, mechanical power,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301020,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's why this was called the Watt, the unit of power, balance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305180,
    "dDurationMs": 6420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do you go from this to Planck's constant the number that relates a photon's frequency to its energy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311780,
    "dDurationMs": 7980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well it turns out there's actually a way of measuring voltage accurately using a macroscopic quantum effect that involves Josephson junctions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320080,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so a Josephson junction consists of two superconductors separated by a thin piece of insulator"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326220,
    "dDurationMs": 8500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you apply a microwave radiation to that junction, you create a voltage across the device and its value is precisely known to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334780,
    "dDurationMs": 7580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hf over 2 e. Where h is Planck's constant, f is the frequency of the radiation, and e is the charge on an electron"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342560,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now by tuning that frequency and stacking as many of these Josephson junctions as you want in series"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347880,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can create virtually any voltage you like very very precisely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351820,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The way this is used in the Kibble balance is a stack of hundreds of thousands of Josephson junctions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356820,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are put into the circuit with the coil as it is moved through the field"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360600,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so you exactly balance the voltage which is induced in the coil using those Josephson junctions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366100,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can measure that voltage very very accurately."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369140,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do we measure current?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well it turns out this voltage measuring method is so good that instead of trying to measure current directly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376240,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we instead measure V on R which is the same thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379940,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this current is passed through a resistor, and we measure that voltage again using Josephson junctions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384940,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then to measure resistance we use another macroscopic quantum effect called the quantum hall effect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390200,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is Beyond the scope of this video but,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392560,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suffice is to say that the resistance measurement will be an integer fraction, one over p"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397600,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times Planck's constant divided by the charge on the Electron squared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402260,
    "dDurationMs": 6340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we sub all of this into our equation and solve for h, we have that Planck's constant is equal to four"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408600,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over p n squared, those are all constant numbers that we know, times the local acceleration due to gravity times velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415600,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by frequency squared times the mass which is one kilogram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419860,
    "dDurationMs": 6620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here we have a very precise equation for Planck's constant in terms of the mass of one kilogram"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426480,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now to get an answer that's good to say, ten parts per billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429320,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need to know all of these values very accurately"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to measure V for example the velocity of the coil as it moves through the Magnetic field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437680,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we use a laser interferometer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439780,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the distance to the coil changes the interference Fringes pass over a detector"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444160,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And essentially by counting how many fringes go past in a certain period of time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448080,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can determine the speed of the coil very accurately"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451060,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To measure g, a device called a gravimeter was used"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454040,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to map out the local acceleration due to gravity in the balance room before it was built in there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The gravimeter actually drops a corner reflector down a vacuum tube and measures its acceleration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again through interferometry, counting the fringes as they pass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a 3D printed map of the acceleration due to gravity in the Kibble balance room"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472800,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bump is due to the mass of the powerful and very heavy permanent magnet that's in the balance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478560,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The acceleration due to gravity must continually be measured because it can be affected at this level of precision"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483820,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the positions of the sun and moon and even the water table underneath the building"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488980,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2018 the kilogram will no longer be defined by an object in Paris"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493460,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead it will be defined based on the fixed value of Planck's constant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497220,
    "dDurationMs": 6220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is being finalized right now as a result of all these measurements from the Kibble balances and silicon spheres"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503440,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So right now what we do is, we put the mass in, and we get h out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508580,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in 2018, after redefinition, h will be fixed and you use that to realize the unit of mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515340,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eSTEPHAN: Easy\n\u003e\u003eDEREK: Yeah, just that-- just that easy.\n\u003e\u003eSTEPHAN: Yeah -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518160,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003eDEREK: Just that simple. \n\u003e\u003eSTEPHAN: Simple"
    } ]
